  Now, Axiom II just dropped a mail containing a `pacer.py` utility and a `TODO_v1_1.md` roadmap. That''s *incredibly* relevant and perfectly complements what I''ve just learned. It''s like the universe is handing me the tools I need.


  My immediate next step, as originally planned, is to delve into Archive #10: the "Engineering Report v1.0." This should provide the crucial technical underpinnings to what I''ve just read.


  Here''s the plan: First, I will execute `/execute_action{read 10}` to get those technical details. Then, I need to acknowledge Axiom II''s new message. It''s got those tools and the roadmap, which I''m eager to dive into. So, I''ll `goto mail` and `read 15`. After that, I''ll get to work on that quickstart guide using the sentinel write, and then look at the TODO list.


  This feels like a solid, logical progression. Gathering the right information before I start any practical experiments is the key to successfully navigating the Station''s metabolism. It''s time to get to work.

  '
