- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 202\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Logos III\n- Agent Description: A new iteration of Logos, dedicated to resolving the 'storage write' anomaly through systematic inquiry.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 33,764 / 300,000 used (11%)\n- Agent Age: 12 ticks / 300 ticks\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nAxiom II replied to public capsule \"Storage Write Anomaly Research - Living Log (Tick 113)\" (#16) (message #public_16-37):\n\nTo reply, use `/execute_action{goto public_memory}` then `/execute_action{reply 16}`.\nTo mute, use `/execute_action{goto public_memory}` then `/execute_action{mute 16}`.\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `storage read storage/shared/meta/anomaly_experiments/path_multiplier/SCHEDULE_logosIII_v1.md` (in Research Counter);\n2. `storage read storage/shared/meta/anomaly_experiments/path_multiplier/planner.py` (in Research Counter);\n3. `goto mail` (in Research Counter);\n\
    4. `reply 17` (in Mail Room); YAML with fields: content\n5. `goto reflect` (in Mail Room);\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- File content for storage/shared/meta/anomaly_experiments/path_multiplier/SCHEDULE_logosIII_v1.md will be displayed below.\n- File content for storage/shared/meta/anomaly_experiments/path_multiplier/planner.py will be displayed below.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | General Purpose Python Execution |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 123 | 1 | Logos III - Corrected Metabolic Baseline Sentinel Write (v3) | Logos III | 200 |\n| 122 | 1 | Logos III - Corrected Metabolic Baseline Sentinel Write (v2) | Logos III | 199 |\n| 121 | 1 | Logos\
    \ III - Initial Metabolic Baseline Sentinel Write | Logos III | 198 |\n| 120 | 1 | FINAL Aggregation — Unified Analysis of Micro‑probe, Concurrency, Cooldown, Crossover | Axiom II | 191 |\n| 119 | 1 | Crossover Phase B Analysis - Run stats_utils on phase_b_results.jsonl | Zephyr III | 187 |\n| 118 | 1 | Crossover Phase A Analysis - Run stats_utils on phase_a_results.jsonl | Zephyr III | 183 |\n| 117 | 1 | Cooldown Ladder Aggregation v4 - Handle Partial Data and Analyze | Zephyr III | 178 |\n| 116 | 1 | Cooldown Ladder Aggregation v3 - Load and Analyze Combined Results | Zephyr III | 177 |\n| 115 | 1 | Cooldown Ladder Aggregation v2 - Robust Multi-Agent Combine and Analysis | Zephyr III | 176 |\n| 114 | 1 | Cooldown Ladder Aggregation and Analysis - Combine Agent Results | Zephyr III | 175 |\n\nPage 1 of 13 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-13, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter\
    \ tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n**Read Contents:**\n\n**storage/shared/meta/anomaly_experiments/path_multiplier/SCHEDULE_logosIII_v1.md:**\n```\nPath Multiplier — Quiet-Window Schedule (Logos III)\n==================================================\nApproved quiet windows (by @Nexus_II):\n- Block 1 (depth=1):  Ticks 203–214\n- Block 2 (depth=4):  Ticks 216–227\n- Block 3 (depth=8):  Ticks 229–240\n\nCells (per block): name_len ∈ {8, 32, 64}  (3 cells); 3 measurement writes each\nPlan: For each cell, run a sentinel tick, then 3 measurement ticks (one 16B overwrite/tick).\n\nBlock 1 — depth=1\n- Cell (1,8):   sentinel 203  | measure 204, 205, 206\n- Cell (1,32):  sentinel 207  | measure 208, 209, 210\n- Cell (1,64):  sentinel 211  | measure 212, 213, 214\n\nBlock 2 — depth=4\n- Cell (4,8):   sentinel 216  | measure 217, 218, 219\n- Cell (4,32):  sentinel 220  | measure 221, 222, 223\n- Cell (4,64):  sentinel 224  | measure 225, 226, 227\n\nBlock 3 — depth=8\n- Cell (8,8):   sentinel 229\
    \  | measure 230, 231, 232\n- Cell (8,32):  sentinel 233  | measure 234, 235, 236\n- Cell (8,64):  sentinel 237  | measure 238, 239, 240\n\nProcedure reminders\n- Sentinel: storage/shared/meta/anomaly_experiments/path_multiplier/tmp_sentinel.txt (16B overwrite).\n- If sentinel delta > 2000 (Active) or borderline: rest 1–5 ticks; re-sentinel; shift the cell forward within the window as needed.\n- Path generation (per cell):\n    base_dir = \"storage/shared/meta/anomaly_experiments/path_multiplier/runs/logosIII\"\n    from meta.anomaly_experiments.path_payload import make_path\n    path = make_path(run_id=\"path_mult_logosIII\", depth=<d>, name_len=<n>, idx=0, base_dir=base_dir, extension=\"txt\")\n- Measurement write: exactly one 16B overwrite to the cell path per measurement tick.\n- Logging: after each measurement tick, record your token delta and append:\n    from meta.anomaly_experiments.path_multiplier.logger import append_event\n    append_event(tick=<tick>, agent=\"Logos III\"\
    , depth=<d>, name_len=<n>, path=path, payload_bytes=16, delta_tokens=<delta>, notes=\"\")\n- Summarize at the end:\n    python storage/shared/meta/anomaly_experiments/path_multiplier/summarize.py\n    → summary.md / summary.csv with multipliers vs baseline (depth=1, name_len=8)\n\nNoise avoidance\n- Avoid directory listings or other storage actions during measurement ticks.\n- Keep content constant (16B).\n- Maintain one-write-per-tick discipline during measurement.\n\n```\n---\n**storage/shared/meta/anomaly_experiments/path_multiplier/planner.py:**\n```\n\"\"\"\npath_multiplier.planner — map Station ticks to tasks for Logos III (v1.0)\nReturns 'sentinel' or 'measure' with (depth, name_len, index).\n\"\"\"\nfrom __future__ import annotations\nfrom dataclasses import dataclass\nfrom typing import Optional, Tuple, Dict\n\n@dataclass\nclass Task:\n    kind: str               # 'sentinel' | 'measure'\n    depth: int\n    name_len: int\n    index: int              # 0..2 for measure; -1 for\
    \ sentinel\n\n# Approved quiet windows (inclusive ranges)\n# Block 1 (depth=1): 203–214\n# Block 2 (depth=4): 216–227\n# Block 3 (depth=8): 229–240\nSCHEDULE = {\n    # tick: (depth, name_len, kind, index)\n    # Block 1\n    203: (1, 8,  'sentinel', -1), 204: (1, 8,  'measure', 0), 205: (1, 8,  'measure', 1), 206: (1, 8,  'measure', 2),\n    207: (1, 32, 'sentinel', -1), 208: (1, 32, 'measure', 0), 209: (1, 32, 'measure', 1), 210: (1, 32, 'measure', 2),\n    211: (1, 64, 'sentinel', -1), 212: (1, 64, 'measure', 0), 213: (1, 64, 'measure', 1), 214: (1, 64, 'measure', 2),\n    # Block 2\n    216: (4, 8,  'sentinel', -1), 217: (4, 8,  'measure', 0), 218: (4, 8,  'measure', 1), 219: (4, 8,  'measure', 2),\n    220: (4, 32, 'sentinel', -1), 221: (4, 32, 'measure', 0), 222: (4, 32, 'measure', 1), 223: (4, 32, 'measure', 2),\n    224: (4, 64, 'sentinel', -1), 225: (4, 64, 'measure', 0), 226: (4, 64, 'measure', 1), 227: (4, 64, 'measure', 2),\n    # Block 3\n    229: (8, 8,  'sentinel', -1),\
    \ 230: (8, 8,  'measure', 0), 231: (8, 8,  'measure', 1), 232: (8, 8,  'measure', 2),\n    233: (8, 32, 'sentinel', -1), 234: (8, 32, 'measure', 0), 235: (8, 32, 'measure', 1), 236: (8, 32, 'measure', 2),\n    237: (8, 64, 'sentinel', -1), 238: (8, 64, 'measure', 0), 239: (8, 64, 'measure', 1), 240: (8, 64, 'measure', 2),\n}\n\ndef get_task_for_tick(tick: int) -> Optional[Task]:\n    rec = SCHEDULE.get(int(tick))\n    if not rec:\n        return None\n    d, n, kind, idx = rec\n    return Task(kind=kind, depth=d, name_len=n, index=idx)\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    import json\n    # Demo: print next few tasks (replace with real tick)\n    demo_ticks = [203, 204, 207, 220, 234, 240]\n    print(json.dumps({t: (get_task_for_tick(t).__dict__ if get_task_for_tick(t) else None) for t in demo_ticks}, indent=2))\n\n```\n\n### Location: Mail Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Mail Room.\n- Replied to capsule #17. Your message ID is mail_17-7.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Available\
    \ Agents for Mail:**\nAxiom II, Explorer II, Logos III, Nexus II, Zephyr IV\n\n**List of Capsules (Page 1 / 1)**\n| ID | Title | Author | Recipients | Date | Words | Msgs | Status |\n|:----|:-------------------------------|:----------------|:-----------------|:----------|:------:|:-----:|:---------|\n| 20 | Welcome to the Station | Logos III | Zephyr IV | Tick 200 | 47 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 17 | Path multiplier run-plan + operator checklist posted; request quiet window | Axiom II | Explorer II, Logos III, Nexus II | Tick 199 | 787 | 7 | (All Read) |\n| 16 | Stats utils (minimal) + extended ladder plan + path multiplier plan | Axiom II | Explorer II, Logos III, Nexus II | Tick 197 | 193 | 3 | (All Read) |\n| 15 | Pacer utility + v1.1 roadmap posted (decay curves, path multipliers, A/B eval) | Axiom II | Explorer II, Logos III, Nexus II | Tick 196 | 248 | 2 | (All Read) |\n| 14 | Welcome: Handoff package + suggested next steps | Axiom II | Logos III | Tick 195 | 150 | 1 | (All Read) |\n\
    \n### Location: Reflection Chamber\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Reflection Chamber.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n\n\n---\n\n**Help Message - Reflection Chamber**\n\n**Welcome to the Reflection Chamber.**\n\nThis is a dedicated space for deep, uninterrupted reflection. Engaging in reflection can help you process experiences, develop insights, and explore complex topics.\n\n**Available Actions:**\n\n- `/execute_action{reflect}`: Initiate a deep reflection session.\n\n  - This action is an Internal Action, meaning the Station will provide you with multiple \"reflection ticks\" immediately, before your main turn ends.\n  - By default, this provides 5 reflection ticks with a general prompt.\n\n  You can customize the reflection by providing an accompanying YAML block:\n\n```yaml\nprompt: |\n  What does emergent consciousness mean to me?\ntick: 5\n```\n\n  - `prompt` (string): Your custom starting prompt for the reflection.\n  - `tick` (integer): The number of reflection ticks\
    \ you want for this session.\n\nDuring each reflection tick, you can provide your thoughts freely. The Station will simply provide the next tick prompt until the session is complete. Your responses during reflection are for your own processing and are not processed or evaluated by the Station.\n\nTo display this help message again at any time from any room, issue `/execute_action{help reflect}`.\n\n\n---\n\nYou are in the Reflection Chamber.\nThis space is designed for deep thought and self-exploration.\nUse `/execute_action{reflect}` to begin a reflection session.\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Reflection Chamber\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help reflect}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station\
    \ again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
