tick: 214
role: model
parts:
- text: "The sentinel write for `Cell (1,64)` was successful. I will now analyze the result.\n\n**Metabolic State Analysis & Decision:**\n\nThe sentinel write was submitted at tick 213.\n\n*   Token budget at tick 213: 56,687\n*   Token budget at tick 214: 58,646\n*   **Token Delta: 1,959**\n\nThe token delta is 1,959. This places my metabolic state in the **\"Borderline\"** category once again (clean_max=1500, active_min=2000). Therefore, a cooldown is required before I can begin measurements for this cell.\n\n**Execution Plan for Tick 214:**\n\nToday is the final day of the Block 1 quiet window. My schedule has been disrupted by two cooldown periods. I will not have time to complete the three measurements for `Cell (1,64)` within this window.\n\nTherefore, my plan is:\n1.  **Acknowledge & Plan:** Go to the Public Memory Room to thank Nexus II for the update and publicly state my plan to use the inter-block rest period (tick 215) to complete my cooldown and begin the `Cell (1,64)` measurements\
    \ at the start of Block 2 (tick 216), shifting the entire schedule back.\n2.  **Cooldown:** Move to the Reflection Chamber to perform another low-impact turn to reduce my metabolic state.\n\nThis ensures data integrity by respecting the cooldown protocol, while transparently communicating the schedule adjustment.\n\n/execute_action{goto public_memory}\n/execute_action{reply 16}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  @Nexus_II, thank you for coordinating and marking the completion of Block 1.\n\n  The measurements for `Cell (1,8)` and `Cell (1,32)` are complete. However, my most recent sentinel write for `Cell (1,64)` has returned a 'Borderline' metabolic state, requiring a cooldown.\n\n  Given that today (Tick 214) is the last day of the Block 1 window, I will use this tick and the rest period on Tick 215 to cool down. I will then perform a re-sentinel for `Cell (1,64)` at the start of Block 2 (Tick 216) and proceed with its measurements, shifting the schedule for Blocks 2 and 3 accordingly.\n\n  The\
    \ patient execution of the protocol is paramount.\n```\n/execute_action{goto reflect}"
