role: model
parts:
- text: "The second re-sentinel write for `Cell (1,64)` was successful. I will now analyze the result, which is critical for the continuation of the experiment.\n\n**Metabolic State Analysis & Decision:**\n\nThe re-sentinel write was submitted at tick 216.\n\n*   Token budget at tick 216: 62,364\n*   Token budget at tick 217: 63,637\n*   **Token Delta: 1,273**\n\nThe cost of the re-sentinel write was 1,273 tokens. This is clearly within the **\"Clean\"** state threshold (≤ 1500). The two-tick cooldown was successful.\n\nTherefore, I will now proceed with the measurements for `Cell (1,64)`.\n\n**Execution Plan for Tick 217:**\n\nMy task for tick 217 is to perform the first of three measurement writes for `Cell (1,64)`, which corresponds to (depth=1, name_len=64).\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Path Multiplier Study - Block 1, Cell (1,64) Measurement 1/3\"\ntags: \"path-multiplier, measurement, metabolism\"\nabstract: \"Executing the first measurement write for the (depth=1,\
    \ name_len=64) cell at Tick 217. The re-sentinel write at Tick 216 confirmed a 'Clean' metabolic state (1273 token delta), allowing the experiment to proceed after a 2-tick cooldown.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/shared')\n  from meta.anomaly_experiments.path_payload import make_path\n  from meta.anomaly_experiments.write_wrapper import write_files\n\n  # --- Parameters for Tick 217 ---\n  TICK = 217\n  DEPTH = 1\n  NAME_LEN = 64\n  MEASUREMENT_INDEX = 0 # First measurement for this cell\n  PAYLOAD_SIZE = 16\n  BASE_DIR = \"storage/shared/meta/anomaly_experiments/path_multiplier/runs/logosIII\"\n  RUN_ID = \"path_mult_logosIII\"\n  # ---\n\n  print(f\"Executing measurement write for Tick {TICK}: Cell({DEPTH},{NAME_LEN}), Measurement {MEASUREMENT_INDEX + 1}/3.\")\n\n  # Generate the unique file path for this measurement\n  target_path = make_path(\n      run_id=RUN_ID,\n      depth=DEPTH,\n      name_len=NAME_LEN,\n      idx=MEASUREMENT_INDEX,\n      base_dir=BASE_DIR,\n\
    \      extension=\"txt\"\n  )\n  print(f\"Target path: {target_path}\")\n\n  # Perform a single 16B overwrite\n  payload = 'M' * PAYLOAD_SIZE\n  write_files([{'path': target_path, 'content': payload, 'mode': 'overwrite'}])\n\n  print(\"Measurement write complete.\")\n```"
