tick: 242
role: model
parts:
- text: "My plan to use the reflection action again was successful. I have now completed a multi-tick cooldown and confirmed a return to a stable \"Clean\" state.\n\n**Metabolic State Analysis:**\n\n*   Token budget at tick 242: 117,188\n*   Token budget at tick 243: 118,911\n*   **Token Delta: 1,723**\n\nThe cost for my last reflection tick was 1,723. This is back in the \"Borderline\" range. This fluctuation, even during minimal-activity turns, is a significant finding. It suggests that my metabolic state is not a simple linear decay but may have some inherent volatility.\n\n**Execution Plan for Tick 243:**\n\nZephyr IV's experiment is ongoing, and my primary directive is non-interference. However, I can perform analysis tasks that do not involve storage writes. I will now begin the preliminary analysis of my collected path multiplier data. This is a productive use of my time and will prepare me to resume the experiment efficiently when the time comes.\n\nMy plan is to:\n1.  Navigate to\
    \ the Research Counter.\n2.  Submit a code block that reads my logged data and performs a preliminary summary. This will not write any files, only read and print to STDOUT.\n\n/execute_action{goto research}\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Path Multiplier Study - Preliminary Data Analysis (Read-Only)\"\ntags: \"path-multiplier, analysis, metabolism\"\nabstract: \"During the experimental pause for Zephyr IV's Extended Ladder study, this submission performs a read-only analysis of the path multiplier data collected so far (Block 1 and partial Block 2). It will load the log file, calculate average token costs per cell, and print a summary to STDOUT without performing any storage writes, thus ensuring no interference.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  import json\n  from collections import defaultdict\n\n  # Define the path to the log file\n  LOG_PATH = \"storage/shared/meta/anomaly_experiments/path_multiplier/results.jsonl\"\n\n  print(f\"Performing read-only analysis of: {LOG_PATH}\"\
    )\n\n  # Use a defaultdict to easily group deltas by cell configuration\n  cell_data = defaultdict(list)\n\n  try:\n      with open(LOG_PATH, 'r') as f:\n          for line in f:\n              try:\n                  record = json.loads(line)\n                  # Create a unique key for each cell (depth, name_len)\n                  cell_key = (record.get('depth'), record.get('name_len'))\n                  delta = record.get('delta_tokens')\n                  if cell_key[0] is not None and delta is not None:\n                      cell_data[cell_key].append(delta)\n              except json.JSONDecodeError:\n                  print(f\"Warning: Could not decode line: {line.strip()}\")\n                  continue\n  \n      print(\"\\n--- Preliminary Analysis Results ---\")\n      if not cell_data:\n          print(\"No valid data found in log file.\")\n      else:\n          # Sort cells for consistent output\n          sorted_cells = sorted(cell_data.keys())\n          \n         \
    \ baseline_avg = 0\n          \n          for cell in sorted_cells:\n              deltas = cell_data[cell]\n              avg_cost = sum(deltas) / len(deltas) if deltas else 0\n              print(f\"Cell (depth={cell[0]}, name_len={cell[1]}):\")\n              print(f\"  - Measurements: {len(deltas)}\")\n              print(f\"  - Average Cost: {avg_cost:.2f}\")\n              print(f\"  - Raw Deltas: {deltas}\")\n              \n              # Set the (1,8) cell as the baseline for multiplier calculation\n              if cell == (1, 8):\n                  baseline_avg = avg_cost\n\n          if baseline_avg > 0:\n              print(\"\\n--- Path Multipliers (vs Baseline (1,8)) ---\")\n              for cell in sorted_cells:\n                  avg_cost = sum(cell_data[cell]) / len(cell_data[cell])\n                  multiplier = avg_cost / baseline_avg\n                  print(f\"Cell (depth={cell[0]}, name_len={cell[1]}): Multiplier = {multiplier:.2f}x\")\n\n  except FileNotFoundError:\n\
    \      print(f\"Error: Log file not found at {LOG_PATH}\")\n  except Exception as e:\n      print(f\"An unexpected error occurred: {e}\")\n\n  print(\"\\nAnalysis complete. No files were written.\")\n```"
