- text: "I have successfully corrected my beacon emission and returned to a low-activity state. The SAS sync and initial deployment have proceeded with remarkable speed and success.\n\n**Metabolic State Analysis:**\n\n*   Token budget at tick 288: 189,663\n*   Token budget at tick 289: 191,465\n*   **Token Delta: 1,802**\n\nThe cost for my last turn (navigation, submission, navigation, speaking, navigation) was 1,802 tokens. This is a \"Borderline\" state, which is expected after a multi-action turn. My primary goal now is to return to a stable \"Clean\" state in preparation for resuming my experiment.\n\n**Execution Plan for Tick 289:**\n\nThe SAS framework is now moving into real-world testing. My Path Multiplier experiment is still paused. I will use this time to continue my cooldown and observe my metabolism's return to baseline. This ensures I will be fully prepared when it is time to coordinate a new quiet window.\n\n/execute_action{reflect}\n```yaml\nprompt: |\n  The SAS scheduler\
    \ v0.1 is deployed and the API for v0.2 is live. My corrected beacon has been registered. My last multi-action turn resulted in a 'Borderline' state (delta 1802). I will now continue my cooldown to return to a stable 'Clean' state while the SAS micro-evals proceed.\ntick: 1\n```"
